# hotkeys.js is gitignored, same as lib/app-hotkeys.ahk on the Windows side — but unlike
# lib/app-hotkeys.ahk, its template (hotkeys.template.js) is an *unsanitized* mirror of it,
# refreshed by dev-scripts/make-template.sh on every commit (see hooks/pre-commit). A git pull
# always brings the real, working config-as-of-the-last-commit along via the template, without
# git ever touching your own local hotkeys.js directly — no merge conflicts, no risk of a pull
# clobbering local edits you haven't committed anywhere, since it's never staged/tracked at all.
linux/kwin/alttabsucks/contents/code/hotkeys.js
*.pub.key
# Hotkeys UI saves keep the previous file as .bak (real URLs/paths)
linux/kwin/alttabsucks/contents/code/hotkeys.js.bak
lib/app-hotkeys.ahk.bak
# Left over from the earlier JSON-based Hotkeys UI (folded back into the files above once, then
# renamed to *.folded-<timestamp>), and its old migration backups
linux/kwin/alttabsucks/contents/code/hotkeys.json*
lib/hotkeys.json*
lib/hotkeys-ui.generated.ahk
lib/app-hotkeys.ahk.pre-ui-migration-*
